EXPERIMENT 33 – DROPDOWN SELECTION USING SELENIUM
AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to automate dropdown selection using the Select class.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the selenium-java (Selenium 4) dependency to pom.xml.
2. Selenium Manager downloads the browser driver automatically.
3. Open the dropdown page and locate the dropdown using By.id("dropdown").
4. Wrap the element in a Select object.
5. Select options using:
   - selectByVisibleText()
   - selectByValue()
   - selectByIndex()
6. After every selection, print the selected option using getFirstSelectedOption() and print the total number of options.
7. Close the browser and stop.
CODE
Exercise33.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select;

public class Exercise33 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();

            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dropdown");

            Select dropdown = new Select(
                driver.findElement(By.id("dropdown"))
            );

            dropdown.selectByVisibleText("Option 1");
            System.out.println("By visible text : " +
                dropdown.getFirstSelectedOption().getText());

            dropdown.selectByValue("2");
            System.out.println("By value        : " +
                dropdown.getFirstSelectedOption().getText());

            dropdown.selectByIndex(1);
            System.out.println("By index        : " +
                dropdown.getFirstSelectedOption().getText());

            System.out.println("Total options   : " +
                dropdown.getOptions().size());

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
Selection Method	Input
selectByVisibleText()	Option 1
selectByValue()	2
selectByIndex()	1

OUTPUT
By visible text : Option 1
By value        : Option 2
By index        : Option 1
Total options   : 3


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to automate dropdown selection using the Select class was executed successfully and the output was verified.
